<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Therese of Saxe-Hildburghausen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1792">1792</a>–<a href="/years/1854">1854</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Therese of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hildburghausen">Hildburghausen</a> was a German princess who married Crown Prince Ludwig of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a> on 12 October 1810, and was Queen of Bavaria from 1825 to 1848. The horse race held for the wedding became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oktoberfest">Oktoberfest</a>, and the meadow where it took place was named the Theresienwiese after her. She was respected for her charitable work and remained Protestant after her marriage.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/therese-of-saxe-hildburghausen.jpg" alt="Therese of Saxe-Hildburghausen" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: After Joseph Karl Stieler · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:K%C3%B6nigin_Therese_von_Bayern_anonym.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
